text":"ம்","lemma":"m","gloss":"imperative suffix"}],"gloss":"eat!"},{"surface":"எனத்","parts":[{"text":"எனத்","lemma":"எனத்","gloss":"saying"}],"gloss":"saying","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தேட்கடுப்பு","parts":[{"text":"தேள்","lemma":"tēḷ","gloss":"scorpion"},{"text":"கடுப்பு","lemma":"kaṭuppu","gloss":"sting"}],"gloss":"scorpion's sting"},{"surface":"அன்ன","parts":[{"text":"அன்ன","lemma":"aṉṉa","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"},{"surface":"நாட்படு","parts":[{"text":"நாள்","lemma":"nāḷ","gloss":"day"},{"text":"படு","lemma":"paṭu","gloss":"made"}],"gloss":"freshly made"},{"surface":"தேறல்","parts":[{"text":"தேறல்","lemma":"tēṟal","gloss":"filtered liquor"}],"gloss":"liquor"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கோண்மீன்","parts":[{"text":"கோண்மீன்","lemma":"கோண்மீன்","gloss":"bright planet"}],"gloss":"bright planet","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அன்ன","parts":[{"text":"அன்ன","lemma":"aṉṉa","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"},{"surface":"பொலங்கலத்து","parts":[{"text":"பொலங்கலத்து","lemma":"பொலங்கலத்து","gloss":"in a golden vessel"}],"gloss":"in a golden vessel","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அளைஇ","parts":[{"text":"அளைஇ","lemma":"அளைஇ","gloss":"having poured"}],"gloss":"having poured","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஊண்முறை","parts":[{"text":"ஊண்","lemma":"uṇ","gloss":"food"},{"text":"முறை","lemma":"muṟai","gloss":"manner"}],"gloss":"manner of feeding"},{"surface":"ஈத்தல்","parts":[{"text":"ஈ","lemma":"ī","gloss":"give"},{"text":"தல்","lemma":"tal","gloss":"verbal noun suffix"}],"gloss":"giving"},{"surface":"அன்றியும்","parts":[{"text":"அன்றி","lemma":"aṉṟi","gloss":"besides"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"besides"},{"surface":"கோண்முறை","parts":[{"text":"கோண்முறை","lemma":"கோண்முறை","gloss":"manner of receiving"}],"gloss":"manner of receiving","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"விருந்திறை","parts":[{"text":"விருந்து","lemma":"viruntu","gloss":"guest"},{"text":"இறை","lemma":"iṟai","gloss":"gift"}],"gloss":"hospitality gifts"},{"surface":"நல்கியோனே","parts":[{"text":"நல்கியோனே","lemma":"நல்கியோனே","gloss":"he indeed bestowed"}],"gloss":"he indeed bestowed","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அந்தரத்து","parts":[{"text":"அந்தரத்து","lemma":"அந்தரத்து","gloss":"of the heavens"}],"gloss":"of the heavens","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அரும்பெறல்","parts":[{"text":"அருமை","lemma":"arumai","gloss":"rare"},{"text":"பெறல்","lemma":"peṟal","gloss":"obtaining"}],"gloss":"rare to obtain"},{"surface":"அமிழ்த","parts":[{"text":"அமிழ்த","lemma":"அமிழ்த","gloss":"nectar"}],"gloss":"nectar","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மன்ன","parts":[{"text":"மன்ன","lemma":"maṉṉa","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கரும்பு","parts":[{"text":"கரும்பு","lemma":"karumpu","gloss":"sugarcane"}],"gloss":"sugarcane"},{"surface":"இவண்","parts":[{"text":"இவண்","lemma":"ivaṇ","gloss":"here"}],"gloss":"here"},{"surface":"தந்தோன்","parts":[{"text":"தந்தோன்","lemma":"தந்தோன்","gloss":"he who brought"}],"gloss":"he who brought","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பெரும்பிறங்கடையே","parts":[{"text":"பெரும்பிறங்கடையே","lemma":"பெரும்பிறங்கடையே","gloss":"at the great illustrious gate"}],"gloss":"at the great illustrious gate","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"Moon-like white umbrella Atiyar chief / curved-ornament Elini's tall gate standing, I, / pale moonlight's dew-falling dawn, / fighting male elephant's footprint-like my hand, / one-faced big kiṇai drum beating, / fear-inspiring kings' difficult fortress conquered, / fat-filled blood's great flow wetness, / terror-possessing tradition's dark battlefields in every, / white-mouthed donkey's low herd yoking, / white millet and horsegram sowing, / 'daily plowman, may you live long greatly!' saying, / having gone, I stood, on that very day, / village-drunk well's broad-leaved moss, / root-resembling tattered clothes removing, straight-bordered / fine-threaded garment making me wear, 'eat!' saying, / scorpion's sting-like fresh liquor, / bright planet-like golden vessel poured, / manner of feeding giving, besides, manner of receiving / hospitality gifts he bestowed, of the heavens / rare to obtain nectar-like / sugarcane here brought-one's great illustrious gate.","translation":"I stood at the tall gate of Elini, the chief of the Atiyar clan who holds a moon-like white umbrella and wears curved ornaments. At the chilly dawn under the pale moonlight, beating my single-faced large kiṇai drum with a hand that looks like the footprint of a fighting male elephant, I sang: 'O plowman who daily yokes a herd of white-mouthed donkeys to plow the dark battlefields of conquered, terrifying kings—wet with the great flow of fat-filled blood—and sows white millet and horsegram there, may you live long!' On that very day, he removed my tattered clothes, which resembled the moss on the broad leaves of a village well, and made me wear a fine-threaded, straight-bordered garment. Saying 'Eat!', he poured fresh liquor, sharp as a scorpion's sting, into a golden vessel that shone like a bright planet. Not only did he feed me generously, but he also bestowed upon me great hospitality gifts. Such is the generosity at the illustrious gate of the descendant of him who brought sugarcane, rare as heavenly nectar, to this world.","modern":"சந்திரன் போன்ற வெண்கொற்றக் குடையை உடைய அதியர் குலத் தலைவனும், வளைந்த அணிகலன்களை அணிந்தவனுமாகிய எழினியினுடைய உயர்ந்த வாயிலில் நான் போய் நின்றேன். பனி விழுகின்ற, மங்கிய நிலவொளி வீசும் அதிகாலைப் பொழுதில், போரிடும் ஆண் யானையின் அடிச்சுவடு போன்ற எனது கையினால், ஒரு பக்கத் தோலையுடைய பெரிய கிணைப் பறையை முழக்கினேன். 'அச்சம் தரும் பகை மன்னர்களின் அரிய கோட்டைகளைக் கைப்பற்றி, கொழுப்பு நிறைந்த குருதி வெள்ளத்தால் ஈரமான போர்க்களங்கள் தோறும், வெண்மையான வாயையுடைய கழுதைகளைப் பூட்டி உழுது, வெள்ளை வரகையும் கொள்ளையும் விதைக்கும் நாள்தோறும் உழும் உழவனே! நீ பல்லாண்டு வாழ்க!' என்று வாழ்த்திப் பாடினேன். நான் அவ்வாறு பாடி நின்ற அன்றே, அவன் ஊரார் உண்ணும் கிணற்றிலுள்ள அகன்ற இலைகளையுடைய பாசியைப் போன்ற எனது கிழிந்த ஆடைகளை நீக்கினான். நேர்த்தியான கரையையுடைய மெல்லிய நூலால் நெய்யப்பட்ட ஆடையை எனக்கு உடுத்தச் செய்தான். 'உண்க!' என்று கூறி, தேளின் கொட்டுதலைப் போன்ற சுவையுடைய புதிய கள்ளினை, விண்மீனைப் போன்ற பொற்கலத்தில் ஊற்றித் தந்தான். உணவளித்ததோடு மட்டுமல்லாமல், முறைப்படி விருந்தினருக்குத் தரும் பரிசில்களையும் தந்து சிறப்பித்தான். விண்ணுலகத்து அமிழ்தம் போன்ற கரும்பை இந்நில உலகிற்கு முதன்முதலில் கொண்டு வந்த முன்னோனின் வழிவந்த அவனது சிறந்த வாயிலில் இத்தகைய கொடை நிகழ்ந்தது.","explanation":"The poet Avvaiyar is praising Poguttelini, the son of the famous patron Adhiyaman Neduman Anji, describing her arrival at his palace gate during a cold dawn. She compares the king to a warrior-plowman who 'plows' the battlefields of defeated enemies using donkeys—a traditional sign of total destruction of an enemy's land—and sows wild grains. In return for her song, the king immediately replaces her moss-like tattered clothes with fine garments, serves her potent fresh liquor in golden cups, and showers her with gifts. The poem belongs to the Pāṭāṇ tiṇai, highlighting the patron's heroism and immense generosity. The closing lines refer to the ancestral glory of the Atiyamāṉ lineage, credited with bringing sugarcane to the Tamil land.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.2],[1.2,1.5],[1.5,1.8],[1.8,3.0],[3.0,3.5],[3.5,3.8],[3.8,4.2],[4.2,4.7],[4.7,5.6],[5.6,5.8],[5.8,6.2],[6.2,6.9],[7.5,7.8],[7.8,8.4],[8.4,9.0],[9.0,9.56],[9.56,9.93],[9.93,10.3],[10.3,10.87],[10.87,11.1],[11.1,12.1],[12.1,12.4],[12.7,13.0],[13.0,13.5],[13.5,14.5],[14.5,14.68],[14.68,15.4],[15.4,15.9],[15.9,16.9],[16.9,17.1],[17.1,17.48],[17.73,18.1],[18.84,19.27],[19.27,19.61],[19.61,20.04],[20.04,20.34],[20.34,21.54],[21.54,21.74],[21.74,21.94],[21.94,22.34],[22.34,23.64],[23.64,23.84],[23.84,24.44],[24.44,24.9],[24.9,25.37],[25.37,26.14],[26.14,26.81],[26.81,27.1],[27.1,27.34],[27.34,28.14],[28.14,28.61],[28.61,29.24],[29.31,29.54],[29.83,30.54],[30.54,30.94],[30.94,31.44],[31.